          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            It is a classical fact that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rationalization"} rationalization
            of classical
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+theory"} homotopy theory
            (of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+spaces"} topological spaces
            or
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+sets"} simplicial sets
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rational+homotopy+theory"} rational homotopy theory
            – is considerably more tractable than general
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+theory"} homotopy theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dg-algebra"} dg-algebraic
            models for
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rational+homotopy+types"} rational homotopy types
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/minimal+Sullivan+algebras"} minimal Sullivan algebras
            or equivalently their
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dual"} dual
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dg-coalgebras"} dg-coalgebras
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+homotopy+theory"} stable homotopy theory
            i.e. the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+theory"} homotopy theory
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectra"} spectra
            (of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+spaces"} topological spaces
            or
            = succeed "):" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+sets"} simplicial sets
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+complexes"} chain complexes
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dg-modules"} dg-modules
            over
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℚ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Q}
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rational+stable+homotopy+theory"} rational stable homotopy theory
            compatible with that of classical rational homotopy theory in tat the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stabilization"} stabilization
            adjunction that connects classical
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+theory"} homotopy theory
            to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+homotopy+theory"} stable homotopy theory
            is, under these identifications, modeled by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/forgetful+functor"} forgetful functor
            from dg-(co-)algebras to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+complexes"} chain complexes
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mtext classical homotopy theory
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mtext stable homotopy theory
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mi spaces
                        %mtd
                          %munderover
                            %mrow
                            %munder
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                                %msup
                                  %mi Σ
                                  %mn ∞
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟵
                              %mrow
                                %msup
                                  %mi Ω
                                  %mn ∞
                        %mtd
                          %mi spectra
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mtext stabilization
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mtext rationally
                        %mtd
                          %mtext dg(co)algebras
                        %mtd
                          %munderover
                            %mrow
                            %munder
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mi underlying
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟵
                              %mi free
                        %mtd
                          %mtext chain complexes
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  \&amp; \text{classical homotopy theory}
                  \&amp;&amp;
                  \\text{stable homotopy theory}
                  \\\
                  \&amp; spaces &amp; \underoverset{\underset{\Sigma^\infty}{\longrightarrow}}{\overset{\Omega^\infty}{\longleftarrow}}{} &amp; spectra
                  \\\
                  \&amp; &amp; \text{stabilization}
                  \\\
                  \\text{rationally}
                  \&amp;
                  \\text{dg(co)algebras}
                  \&amp;
                  \\underoverset{\underset{underlying}{\longrightarrow}}{\overset{free}{\longleftarrow}}{}
                  \&amp;
                  \\text{chain complexes}
                  }
          %p
            Classical
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+theory"} homotopy theory
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+homotopy+theory"} stable homotopy theory
            are unified and jointly generalized in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/parameterized+stable+homotopy+theory"} parameterized stable homotopy theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/objects"} objects
            are
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/parameterized+spectra"} parameterized spectra
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type"} homotopy type
            %em rational parameterized stable homotopy theory
            to be discussed here is supposed to be the rationalization of this joint generalization, unifiying and jointly generalizing the algebraic model of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rational+topological+spaces"} rational topological spaces
            by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sullivan+algebras"} Sullivan algebras
            and of
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi H
                    %mi ℚ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H \mathbb{Q}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/module+spectra"} module spectra
            by
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+complexes"} chain complexes
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mtext stable homotopy theory
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mtext parameterized stable homotopy theory
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mtext classical homotopy theory
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mtext spectra
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo ⟶
                            %mphantom
                              %mtext include
                        %mtd
                          %mtext parameterized spectra
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo ⟶
                            %mphantom
                              %mtext project
                        %mtd
                          %mtext spaces
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mtext include
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mtext project
                        %mtd
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mtext rationally
                        %mtd
                          %mtext chain complexes
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo ⟶
                            %mphantom
                              %mtext include
                        %mtd
                          %mtext dg-modules
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo ⟶
                            %mphantom
                              %mtext project
                        %mtd
                          %mtext dg(co)algebras
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  \&amp; \text{stable homotopy theory}
                  \&amp;&amp;
                  \\text{parameterized stable homotopy theory}
                  \&amp;&amp;
                  \\text{classical homotopy theory}
                  \\\
                  \&amp;
                  \\text{spectra}
                  \&amp;\overset{\phantom{\text{include}}}{\longrightarrow}&amp;
                  \\text{parameterized spectra}
                  \&amp;\overset{\phantom{\text{project}}}{\longrightarrow}&amp;
                  \\text{spaces}
                  \\\
                  \&amp;
                  \&amp;\text{include}&amp;
                  \&amp;\text{project}&amp;
                  \\\
                  \\text{rationally}
                  \&amp;
                  \\text{chain complexes}
                  \&amp;\overset{\phantom{\text{include}}}{\longrightarrow}&amp;
                  \\text{dg-modules}
                  \&amp;\overset{\phantom{\text{project}}}{\longrightarrow}&amp;
                  \\text{dg(co)algebras}
                  }
          %p
            Here we (intend to) show that, accordingly, rational parameterized homotopy theory is presented by the the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/opposite+category"} opposite
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopical+category"} homotopical category
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dg-modules"} dg-modules
            over cochain
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+graded-commutative+algebras"} differential graded-commutative algebras
            in non-negative degrees.
