          %h2#references References
          %p
            A classical reference on plain
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rational+homotopy+theory"} rational homotopy theory
            is:
          %ul
            %li#BousfieldGugenheim76
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Aldridge+Bousfield"}> Aldridge Bousfield
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Victor+Gugenheim"} Victor Gugenheim
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/On+PL+deRham+theory+and+rational+homotopy+type"} On PL deRham theory and rational homotopy type
              %strong 179
              (1976) &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://bookstore.ams.org/memo-8-179"}> ams:memo-8-179
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            The equivalence between
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi H
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H R
